hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to tell  edition of ask Evan today we're going to  be continuing our challenge series where  we answer questions from our readers to  help them grow their business so today's  question comes in from Augustine who's  one of the Telus talks business Facebook  fans and Augustine wrote in saying I  want to know how one can run a business  without having to get alone so thanks to  the question Augustine great question  one I know a lot of entrepreneurs are  going through and thinking about how do  I start this business out having to get  money and I used to be in the venture  capital world where I helped raise  capital fractures but I'm actually a big  believer in bootstrapping and trying to  get it done without having to go and  raise money so in this video I'm going  to share three of my top tips to help  you and I look forward to seeing you at  the end of the video number one start  with a surface I almost always  recommended entrepreneurs start a  service-based business you can have  bigger ambitions to create products but  the best way to start is usually through  a service one of the main reasons is the  cost you don't need as much money to  start or maintain a service-based  business often the only thing you need  is your time you don't need an office  you don't need an inventory you don't  need storage you need less equipment if  any and any money you make goes right  into your pocket the first step in  building a successful business is  getting beyond the survival phase and  you have to make enough money to pay  your bills and survive a service-based  business can get the cash flow coming in  more quickly and can allow you to create  a solid base from which you can launch  products if that's your end goal here is  some advice from Tony Robbins the  defining factor is never resources it's  resourceful pneus  number to build around the customer  another great way to build your business  without going into debt is to talk to  your potential customers before you  start interview them ask them what their  pain points are and see if you can find  a way to help them ask them if you could  solve their problem for them what they  hire you if you can start your business  with a customer from day one you're  ahead of the game and have money coming  in the door from the beginning in my  first real business we build software  and spent countless days building a tool  that we thought would be valuable but it  turns out that our clients didn't really  care about it luckily we had enough  other great things in our software that  our clients still bought from us but we  learned our lesson always talk to your  customers to build around them before  you launch here's some advice from Mark  Cuban of course I was underestimated I  was young and this was a new industry I  just used it to my advantage I had more  energy I didn't have any preconceived  notions and how things should be I just  tried to learn technology better than  anyone else and find the best ways to  help my customers number three don't  spend until you earn anybody can spend  money it's easy forgive me million  dollars i'm sure you can find a million  different ways to spend it the hard part  about running a business is making money  i personally hate spending money until  i'm making money i'll invest my time but  i won't put dollars in until I figured  out a model that works here's a quick  example I always wanted to get into  making YouTube videos to answer people's  questions so I could help a wider  audience but didn't have a way to  monetize it so I didn't want to go out  and spend the money on the camera tripod  lighting microphone editor and so on so  I bootstrapped it I used the camera had  at home bouncing on a bookshelf and  recorded the first videos I made were  terrible the content was pretty good and  people still watched him today on  YouTube and give great feedback but the  production quality was brutal I could  have gone out and bought the equipment I  didn't want to spend the money until I  found a way to make money so I kept at  it and eventually discovered a model  that worked then his money came in i was  able to slowly invest into better  equipment and the quality got better the  other benefit here is that i'm only  spending money on something that I know  books and they want to continue doing I  could have bought all the equipment  found out after a few videos that I  don't want to do this and we have  thousands of dollars sitting in my  closet never been used my boot strapping  you find what works and what you want to  continue doing then you spend money to  expand once you found the model that  works here's some advice from lillian  vernon work hard that's the bottom line  don't spend more money than you've got  don't spend money before you've got it  thank you for joining me for another  edition of ask Evan if you like the  video you want to see more please give  it a thumbs up below it always makes me  want to do more of these videos for you  and also love to hear what you have to  think you want to leave a comment under  the video if you have something to say  about this video or some recommendations  for Augustine or if you have a question  for your own business that we can  potentially feature in an upcoming video  feel free to leave in the comments below  I always read those and I try to respond  as soon as I can so thank you and we'll  see you in the next episode  you
 

